= Conclusions and Outlook <ch:conclusion>

Close the loop you opened in @ch:introduction: what was the gap, what did the
work contribute, and what is still open.

== What was done

The theory of @ch:theory and the measurements of @ch:results are the two
halves of the argument. State the result once, plainly, and resist the urge to
repeat the whole thesis here.

== Limitations

Say what the work does _not_ show. A limitation you name yourself is a sign of
control; one your examiner names for you is not.

== Outlook

Point at the next experiment, not at "future work in general".

